<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hasdrubal Gisco</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 202 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hasdrubal Gisco was a Carthaginian general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a> who fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a> until Scipio defeated him at Ilipa in 206 BCE. He won King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syphax">Syphax</a> of the Masaesyli for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> by marrying him to his daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sophonisba">Sophonisba</a>. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> Scipio burned his and Syphax's camps in 203 BCE, and he died soon afterwards.</p></div>
